  "synthesis": "The activity consists of six preprints dated 2026-10-18 to 2026-10-23, spanning chromosome-level genome assemblies and resource databases. Items include a Palythoa comparative genomics study that links transposable element and retrotransposon content to genome size across zooxanthellate and azooxanthellate species, a multi-omics database covering 327 cnidarian species (CnidoSite), and a curated arthropod cuticle protein resource (Cuticulome.org). Genome reports cover the medicinal leech Hirudo verbana (177.66 Mb, 14 scaffolds, 17,789 gene models), the social wasp Belonogaster juncea (315.8 Mb, scaffold N50 7.91 Mb, 573 caste-biased genes), and the nematode Panagrellus redivivus (97.1% BUSCO, 17,839 genes). The signal shows a rise ratio of 3.0 with no published, code, or industry activity and zero 7-day star gain. The available data do not establish a cause for this rise, which reflects preprint volume alone.",
